  "concept_density": "high",
  "scope_boundary": "This chapter covers the Fundamental Rights enshrined in Part III of the Indian Constitution (Articles 12 to 35). It includes definition of State, features, specific rights (equality, freedom, against exploitation, religion, cultural/educational, constitutional remedies), exceptions (Articles 31A-31C), martial law, and criticism. It does not cover Directive Principles of State Policy or other parts of the Constitution in depth, except where mentioned. The right to property (originally Article 31) is discussed as a repealed fundamental right, now under Article 300A.",
